## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design CKNE-aware real-time scheduling for multi-tenant streaming, focusing on dynamic backpressure, fairness, and latency SLAs.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-based rate shaping and budgets
- Token bucket backpressure per tenant
- Dynamic shard/windowing allocation
- Latency SLA preservation and telemetry

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal token bucket sketch
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  consume(n=1){
    const now = Date.now();
    const delta = (now - this.last) * this.rate / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + delta);
    this.last = now;
    if(this.tokens >= n){ this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test starvation scenarios when many tenants drop CKNE to near-zero?
- How would you handle new tenants with no historical CKNE data?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to translate CKNE into concrete tracing budgets and fairness guarantees in a real backend.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE mapping to sampling, retention, storage tier
- Minute-level reallocation with safety guards
- Observability of SLA, budgets, and rollbacks

## Code Example
```javascript
function budgets(ckne, base, max){
  const rate = base + ckne*(max-base);
  const reten = base + ckne*(max-base);
  const hot = base + ckne*(1-base);
  return {rate, reten, hot};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for edge CKNE values and abrupt CKNE shifts?
- What failure modes require automated rollback and how would you detect them?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses understanding of CKNE mapping to multi-tenant compute budgets and how to implement a fair, latency-bounded scheduler.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-concurrency mapping
- Baseline SLA guarantees
- Minute-by-minute rebalancing
- Telemetry and fairness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Allocation function example
function allocateBudget(tenants, totalUnits){
  const base=1; // base per-tenant
  const sumCKNE=tenants.reduce((a,t)=>a+t.ckne,0);
  const alloc={};
  tenants.forEach(t=>{ alloc[t.id]= base + (t.ckne/sumCKNE)*(totalUnits - tenants.length*base);});
  return alloc;
}
```

